OL,3,AGovernments 'asleep at the wheel' over
OL,4,Asocial care, says head of review
OL,5,
OL,6,FSuccessive governments have been
OL,7,F"asleep at the wheel" on adult social
OL,8,Fcare, says the head of the independent
OL,9,Fcommission looking into the sector in
OL,10,FEngland.
OL,12,FBaroness Louise Casey said care
OL,13,Fservices for older people and adults
OL,14,Fwith disabilities had been developed in
OL,15,Fa largely uncontrolled and unintended
OL,16,Fway, unlike the deliberate design of
OL,17,Fthe NHS in 1948.
OL,19,FAs a result, she suggested a postcode
OL,20,Flottery had developed with different
OL,21,Flevels of services available depending
OL,22,Fon where people live.
OL,23,APub: 11-NovQppppppppppppppppppppppG1/2
OL,24,ANext PageB Nat NewsC Nat TVF Clean Feed
